                        "form": "der Willensfreiheit"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "1f8fa60c-a068-406e-be35-b72ebd09a9a8",
                        "entry_id": "1a212789-4800-30a2-a29a-f9d7bf43d7fe",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "singular"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Willensfreiheit"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "374907ba-c3ce-339f-9f77-ec387d684388",
                        "entry_id": "1a212789-4800-30a2-a29a-f9d7bf43d7fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "der Umstand, dass man sich nach eigenem Willen frei entscheiden und danach handeln kann"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Theologie"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "56215ee4-0fc8-47cc-b5bb-d2a851766e02",
                                "sense_id": "374907ba-c3ce-339f-9f77-ec387d684388",
                                "text": "Die Willensfreiheit unterscheidet uns Menschen vom Tier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ccf7b572-6560-4578-a481-f032a33c9116",
                                "sense_id": "374907ba-c3ce-339f-9f77-ec387d684388",
                                "text": "„Deswegen sind es inzwischen nicht mehr Philosophen, sondern Neurowissenschaftler, Biochemiker und Hirnforscher, die fundierte Aussagen über die Willensfreiheit des Menschen machen.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f121baa1-ca50-4f13-b019-bf2bde8e8ad0",
                        "source_entry_id": "1a212789-4800-30a2-a29a-f9d7bf43d7fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "374907ba-c3ce-339f-9f77-ec387d684388",
                        "target_lang_word": "free will",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "free will",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                        "entry_id": "6f5bd4f9-5458-3dcf-b476-d8a5a1a425f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Voluntary choice; (the power of) unforced, uncoerced choice."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f80f8af-4bba-497f-b9a8-d05ee0528da0",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "(insane/worst/best/amazing) use of free will"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de6e1efe-e420-4b95-add3-e2d33c6896a6",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "He did not say it of his own free will, but because his captors coerced him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2f9bf88-a8fb-4412-a01d-18ebf436055e",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "They bound my limbs, depriving me of my free will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb0efea0-20ca-46e5-be42-74fa7005b07d",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "I say therefore, there is no likelyhood, we should imagine, the beasts doe the very same things by a naturall inclination and forced genuitie, which we doe of our owne freewil and industrie."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6ca75d20-4f82-4dc8-9c85-2432eb8490f5",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "Good my Lord, / To come thus was I not constrain'd, but did it / On my free-will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "259d66c5-4f6a-471c-b92d-7cf16ca09c64",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "I make a decree, that all they of the people of Israel, and of his priests and Levites, in my realm, which are minded of their own freewill to go up to Jerusalem, go with thee."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7de6fb73-ebdc-457c-817e-b9b5000dd30a",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "I am impelled to this course by no one, but follow it of my own free-will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4108d585-a343-439a-b904-99bb0b6f8020",
                                                "sense_id": "1efddf50-c271-32cc-898a-54b78ed78343",
                                                "text": "We were faced with a great many problems at Potsdam. The most troublesome one was the refugee problem. They were coming- German refugees were coming from Czechoslovakia and then from Poland into Germany. And Stalin said they weren't coming. We explained to him that they were coming, and they were coming from the countries which he occupied. And then he said they were coming of their own free will and accord. Well, if they came of their own free will- he was just lying about it because they were not coming of their own free will. The same kind of free will affected my grandmother when the Federals ran off with her farm and the goods and things on it, and forced her to move off the farm. These people were forced to move and the Russians were doing it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d9383f04-20e7-375f-bc77-904d0b3b5644",
                                        "entry_id": "6f5bd4f9-5458-3dcf-b476-d8a5a1a425f4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The ability to choose one's actions and make choices that are not predetermined by predestination, fate, etc."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9bb8dbd-bd69-44c7-bdd3-48f117760d4d",
                                                "sense_id": "d9383f04-20e7-375f-bc77-904d0b3b5644",
                                                "text": "Some people deny that humans have free will, and argue that every thought and action is preordained by God."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e7fc08f8-fdb0-4599-841d-2c77990e8464",
                                                "sense_id": "d9383f04-20e7-375f-bc77-904d0b3b5644",
                                                "text": "You can bind my limbs, but you can never deprive me of my free will."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2396fd60-3c52-43ed-b295-e97f433736ef",
                                                "sense_id": "d9383f04-20e7-375f-bc77-904d0b3b5644",
                                                "text": "What is free will but the power of volition and action, and of thought and speech, to all appearance as of one's self?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21b2d73a-29c1-48de-a1bd-c99c2f315235",
                                                "sense_id": "d9383f04-20e7-375f-bc77-904d0b3b5644",
                                                "text": "The new challenge to free will comes from a different direction: neuroscience's discovery that people's brains are a collection of diversely oriented modules, and that our understanding of our own intentionality is to a great degree a legitimating fiction which one module in the left hemisphere of the brain retroactively imposes over the decisions different modules make."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cf267c8c-04a5-436a-86cd-55af0dc54c8a",
                        "source_entry_id": "1a212789-4800-30a2-a29a-f9d7bf43d7fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "374907ba-c3ce-339f-9f77-ec387d684388",
                        "target_lang_word": "libre arbitre de la volonté",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6e6aaaf1-a2e4-4515-af91-3eb9bcdf57b1",
                        "source_entry_id": "1a212789-4800-30a2-a29a-f9d7bf43d7fe",
                        "source_sense_id": "374907ba-c3ce-339f-9f77-ec387d684388",
                        "target_lang_word": "libre arbitre",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "libre arbitre",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f195e2f3-26e9-3a6e-acdc-ae0616d06721",
                                        "entry_id": "bdda8ff1-d434-38b6-b5b9-326c3bfc137b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Faculté par laquelle la volonté se détermine à une chose plutôt qu’à une autre indépendamment des déterminations extérieures à elle-même."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8880404-0eb4-4927-a957-0209729f09cc",
                                                "sense_id": "f195e2f3-26e9-3a6e-acdc-ae0616d06721",
                                                "text": "C’est dans cette révision supérieure de la passion par la raison que réside ce que les moralistes ont improprement appelé « le libre arbitre »."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c93ba107-30a5-4e2e-97f7-2300c3d9f276",
                                                "sense_id": "f195e2f3-26e9-3a6e-acdc-ae0616d06721",
                                                "text": "Débusquer les bases biologiques d’un comportement n’enlève rien à l’humanisme du geste ni au libre arbitre : nous demeurons toujours libres de choisir entre un geste altruiste ou égoïste."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02eed7d2-90a5-4470-a37a-17d06ea542fc",
                                                "sense_id": "f195e2f3-26e9-3a6e-acdc-ae0616d06721",
                                                "text": "En politique, on peut partager certaines valeurs avec un parti ou un candidat tout en gardant son libre arbitre. Les raisons qui motivent une personne à voter pour un parti ou un autre ne sont pas homogènes et il est rare qu’on partage 100 % des idées d’un candidat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77113b26-71fa-4420-b639-67aa22fe5602",
                                                "sense_id": "f195e2f3-26e9-3a6e-acdc-ae0616d06721",
                                                "text": "La violence est un acte qui résulte d’une décision prise par la personne qui le commet. Le libre arbitre est l’un des attributs essentiels de la dignité humaine. Si la violence est un choix, il est possible de ne pas être violent. Il suffit de renoncer à la volonté de puissance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "394f2c40-b616-4ed4-bc29-a9c21d2d6497",
                                                "sense_id": "f195e2f3-26e9-3a6e-acdc-ae0616d06721",
                                                "text": "Malgré les progrès substantiels qu'ils ont permis en matière de liberté d'expression, les réseaux sociaux mettent en place toutes les conditions d'un déterminisme algorithmique qui s'oppose insidieusement à notre libre arbitre."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2de01fdc-6608-4212-b2ac-77c1977a17e0",
                        "source_entry_id": "1a212789-4800-30a2-a29a-f9d7bf43d7fe",
